                <pb facs="0335" n="331" sameAs="frus:frus1938v03/pg331"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/14174: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Canton</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Linnell</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Canton</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-10-22T14:30:00+08:00">October 22, 1938—2:30
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received October 22—7 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>4. Two cars with Japanese officers and two lorries with Japanese troops came to
                    British and French bridges of Shameen at 2 p.m. today. Japanese officers saluted
                    and shook hands with the British Concession Chief of Police and then went on to
                    the city. Planes are flying low covering the entry.</p>
                <p>Repeated Chungking, Peiping, Hong Kong.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Linnell</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
